  "id": "randomization-test",
  "term": "randomization test",
  "definition": "A randomization test is a statistical method that builds a reference distribution by calculating the study result across all possible random arrangements allowed by the design. The observed result is then compared with that distribution to estimate a p-value, without relying on standard distributional assumptions such as symmetry or normality.",
